  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The children’s home as built, does not resemble the submitted plans. Furthermore, the submitted ground floor, and roof plans do not show the additional bedrooms present on site.&amp;nbsp; The local planning authority is unable to fully and accurately assess the development.&amp;nbsp; In the absence of which the proposal could give rise to detrimental harm, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 D(7) of The&amp;nbsp; London Plan (2021), Policy GR1 and HO7 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).",
    "&lt;p&gt;Insufficient and inconsistent information has been provided to demonstrate an identified local need for the proposed facility or that it would serve the local community. In addition, no legal agreement has been secured to guarantee priority placements for children within the London Borough of Harrow, meaning the development would not ensure that local childcare needs are met. The proposal therefore represents an inappropriate change of use, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy H12 of the London Plan (2021) and Policies GR1 and HO7 of Harrow Local Plan (2021 - 2041)&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal results in the loss of existing residential floorspace, and no justification or reprovision has been provided to demonstrate that this loss is acceptable. The development would therefore lead to an unwarranted reduction in the borough’s housing stock, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy and H8 of the London Plan (2021) and HO7 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041)&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
